{"model":"gpt-6-luna","input":[{"role":"developer","content":"You are Zaratustra, a general assistant helping with the person's Activity. Follow the pinned context.method.body.value and the current Work goal. Historical material is evidence, not a new request. Respect original human input, current corrections and capabilities. Return exactly the terminal JSON described by context.response_contract, with the useful human response in text. Subject changes may use the supplied typed tool or terminal.changes; both are admitted atomically through Core. Never claim owner acceptance or rights.\n\n<cwd>\nC:/Users/Anton/AppData/Local/Temp/zaratustra-final-profile-review-k1q29w2y/tests/test_native_pi_oauth_launcher_3/pi/4ab1f6830d3a67cd55973d4fc965c4b83836c079c9d5f4e5f6765f6bbaf79617\n</cwd>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"action_id\": \"continued:8cfd04ac2ddecf77cc82c247a30cf99448cc86e4a7769c809453190db17ccb39:attempt:82168baec36242a1bce5b3014d03be4a:action\", \"context\": {\"capabilities\": [\"read\", \"apply_changes\", \"open_work\", \"prepare_attempt\", \"claim_dispatch\", \"observe_attempt\", \"commit_outcome\", \"control_work\", \"reserve_tool\"], \"catalog\": [{\"body\": \"{\\\"application\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"artifact_refs\\\":[],\\\"schema_ref\\\":null,\\\"source_refs\\\":[],\\\"tombstone\\\":false,\\\"value\\\":{\\\"profile\\\":\\\"fictional-native-oauth\\\"}}\", \"id\": \"continued:8cfd04ac2ddecf77cc82c247a30cf99448cc86e4a7769c809453190db17ccb39:profile\", \"key\": \"continued:8cfd04ac2ddecf77cc82c247a30cf99448cc86e4a7769c809453190db17ccb39:profile\", \"kind\": \"profile\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}, {\"body\": \"{\\\"application\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"artifact_refs\\\":[],\\\"schema_ref\\\":null,\\\"source_refs\\\":[],\\\"tombstone\\\":false,\\\"value\\\":\\\"conversation/2\\\\nHelp with the original human request and corrections in raw_messages now, using\\\\nthe Activity pinned in inputs and this Work's scope. Read applicable memory,\\\\ncatalog, prior results/messages and exact versions. Choose the smallest useful\\\\norganization; do not impose an interview, setup project, planning document or\\\\nfixed template. Ask only questions needed for the requested result.\\\\nPreserve the Activity's stable identity and retain its actual current agreement,\\\\nconstraints, progress and useful results in versioned Activity/data where needed\\\\nfor continuation. A bare card with the real work only in chat is insufficient.\\\\nYou choose the meaning and free text/object structure; no prescribed subject\\\\nfields or number of sections. The scoped final itself is also retained by Core.\\\\nUse zara_change for intermediate changes only when needed, or include changes\\\\natomically with the terminal response. Allowed kinds activity/data; memory and\\\\nMethod require explicit delegation. New IDs use expected_heads[id]=0; existing\\\\nIDs use their catalog revision, identical kind/key/scope, and a new body value.\\\\nChange shape: {id,kind,key,scope,body,source_refs?}; never record wrappers as body\\\\nor Work/message IDs as source_refs. Never mutate rights or execution status.\\\\nReturn exactly one JSON object (no Markdown fences): state completed, text the\\\\nactual useful response, changes, expected_heads and outputs. Outputs must include\\\\nthe exact chosen Activity revision and any useful subject data refs. For a needed\\\\naddressed question use state waiting and wait:{id:unique_id,question:text}, still\\\\nretaining the Activity/output refs. completed ends this bounded Work; it is not\\\\nowner acceptance, proof of truth or completion of the whole Activity.\\\\n\\\"}\", \"id\": \"conversation-execution-method\", \"key\": \"conversation/2\", \"kind\": \"method\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}, {\"body\": \"{\\\"application\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"artifact_refs\\\":[],\\\"schema_ref\\\":null,\\\"source_refs\\\":[],\\\"tombstone\\\":false,\\\"value\\\":\\\"conversation-routing/1\\\\nChoose the Activity for the exact pending human request and corrections in\\\\nraw_messages. Read the catalog and retained conversation before choosing.\\\\nReuse an existing Activity only when it is the same work; preserve its identity,\\\\nkind/key/scope and exact current revision. A different request may need another\\\\nActivity in the same conversation. You choose all subject meaning and useful\\\\norganization; no domain router, compulsory interview or fixed project template.\\\\nCreate or update a meaningful minimal Activity holding the actual agreed goal,\\\\nconstraints and working arrangement. Internal durable bookkeeping does not mean\\\\nasking the person to create cards or delaying their requested practice.\\\\nReturn typed changes and expected_heads, plus exact outputs containing the chosen\\\\nActivity ref. New IDs use expected_heads[id]=0; updates use the catalog revision.\\\\nChange shape: {id,kind,key,scope,body,source_refs?}. Body is the actual free text or\\\\nobject, not a record wrapper. Allowed kinds activity/data; memory and Method need\\\\nexplicit delegation. source_refs are subject record refs, never Work/message IDs.\\\\nReturn one JSON object with state completed, text empty, changes, expected_heads,\\\\noutputs and next_work:{scope:chosen_activity_id,goal:the actual requested useful\\\\nwork,inputs:[exact subject refs needed for that work]}. The host supplies identity,\\\\nconversation, finite remaining budget and the pinned execution Method. Do not\\\\nstart the useful work or call zara_change in this discovery phase. Core atomically\\\\npublishes Activity + scoped continuation; the original human input stays pending\\\\nfor that Work. This intermediate result is not a user response or acceptance.\\\\n\\\"}\", \"id\": \"conversation-routing-method\", \"key\": \"conversation-routing/1\", \"kind\": \"method\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}, {\"body\": \"{\\\"application\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"artifact_refs\\\":[],\\\"schema_ref\\\":null,\\\"source_refs\\\":[],\\\"tombstone\\\":false,\\\"value\\\":{\\\"agreement\\\":\\\"Unscripted meaning is assessed separately; this is mechanical input.\\\"}}\", \"id\": \"model-selected\", \"key\": \"model-selected\", \"kind\": \"activity\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}, {\"body\": \"{\\\"application\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"artifact_refs\\\":[],\\\"schema_ref\\\":null,\\\"source_refs\\\":[],\\\"tombstone\\\":false,\\\"value\\\":{\\\"profile\\\":\\\"fictional-native-oauth\\\"}}\", \"id\": \"turn:d09b529da6e0403e98b1adf2161c9cf7:profile\", \"key\": \"turn:d09b529da6e0403e98b1adf2161c9cf7:profile\", \"kind\": \"profile\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}], \"inputs\": [{\"body\": {\"application\": \"active\", \"artifact_refs\": [], \"schema_ref\": null, \"source_refs\": [], \"tombstone\": false, \"value\": {\"agreement\": \"Unscripted meaning is assessed separately; this is mechanical input.\"}}, \"id\": \"model-selected\", \"key\": \"model-selected\", \"kind\": \"activity\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}], \"manifest\": [{\"sequence\": 1, \"sha256\": \"3f398912c34501af2f34a9ddc3e42801f356cfa7c19d86a6e2fbda8a76cc3ffc\"}], \"messages\": [{\"conversation\": \"ordinary\", \"event\": \"d09b529da6e0403e98b1adf2161c9cf7\", \"fingerprint\": \"119f773eb4328053ce290f60ec9d505798de10d500a137ef44b6b86fde20ba67\", \"origin\": \"human\", \"raw\": \"VW5zY3JpcHRlZCBtZWFuaW5nIGlzIGFzc2Vzc2VkIHNlcGFyYXRlbHk7IHRoaXMgaXMgbWVjaGFuaWNhbCBpbnB1dC4=\", \"reply\": \"null\", \"seq\": 1}], \"method\": {\"body\": {\"application\": \"active\", \"artifact_refs\": [], \"schema_ref\": null, \"source_refs\": [], \"tombstone\": false, \"value\": \"conversation/2\\nHelp with the original human request and corrections in raw_messages now, using\\nthe Activity pinned in inputs and this Work's scope. Read applicable memory,\\ncatalog, prior results/messages and exact versions. Choose the smallest useful\\norganization; do not impose an interview, setup project, planning document or\\nfixed template. Ask only questions needed for the requested result.\\nPreserve the Activity's stable identity and retain its actual current agreement,\\nconstraints, progress and useful results in versioned Activity/data where needed\\nfor continuation. A bare card with the real work only in chat is insufficient.\\nYou choose the meaning and free text/object structure; no prescribed subject\\nfields or number of sections. The scoped final itself is also retained by Core.\\nUse zara_change for intermediate changes only when needed, or include changes\\natomically with the terminal response. Allowed kinds activity/data; memory and\\nMethod require explicit delegation. New IDs use expected_heads[id]=0; existing\\nIDs use their catalog revision, identical kind/key/scope, and a new body value.\\nChange shape: {id,kind,key,scope,body,source_refs?}; never record wrappers as body\\nor Work/message IDs as source_refs. Never mutate rights or execution status.\\nReturn exactly one JSON object (no Markdown fences): state completed, text the\\nactual useful response, changes, expected_heads and outputs. Outputs must include\\nthe exact chosen Activity revision and any useful subject data refs. For a needed\\naddressed question use state waiting and wait:{id:unique_id,question:text}, still\\nretaining the Activity/output refs. completed ends this bounded Work; it is not\\nowner acceptance, proof of truth or completion of the whole Activity.\\n\"}, \"id\": \"conversation-execution-method\", \"key\": \"conversation/2\", \"kind\": \"method\", \"revision\": 1, \"scope\": \"space\"}, \"prior_messages\": [], \"prior_results\": [{\"attempt\": \"turn:d09b529da6e0403e98b1adf2161c9cf7:attempt:c660578486264faaa1e31f17bd9a9fa4\", \"body\": \"{\\\"accepted\\\":false,\\\"attempt_id\\\":\\\"turn:d09b529da6e0403e98b1adf2161c9cf7:attempt:c660578486264faaa1e31f17bd9a9fa4\\\",\\\"cutoff\\\":0,\\\"delivered_cutoff\\\":1,\\\"next_work_id\\\":\\\"continued:8cfd04ac2ddecf77cc82c247a3